Q1) A user is not banned (`isBanned = false`). Check if they can login by negating `isBanned` using `!`.

```js
let isBanned = false;
let canLogin = !isBanned
console.log("Can login?",canLogin)
```

Q2) A task is not completed (`isCompleted = false`). Check if it is still pending using `!`.

```js
let isCompleted = false;
let stillPending = !isCompleted
console.log("Is task still pending?",stillPending)
```

Q3) A light is on (`isOn = true`). Check if it is off using `!`.

```js
let isOn = true;
let isOff = !isOn
console.log("Is the light off?",isOff)
```

Q4) A subscription is not active (`isActive = false`). Check if the user cannot access premium content using `!`.

```js
let isActive = false;
let cannotAccess = !isActive
console.log("User cannot access premium?",cannotAccess)
```

Q5) A file is not read‑only (`isReadOnly = false`). Check if it can be edited using `!`.

```js
let isReadOnly = false;
let canBeEdited = !isReadOnly;
console.log("canBeEdited")
```

## Additional Questions

Q6) Predict the output:

```js
let a = 0;
let b = 1;
console.log(!a, !b);
// Output: true, false
```

Q7) Predict the output:

```js
let x = "Hello";
let y = "";
console.log(!x, !y);
// Output: false, true
```

Q8) Predict the output:

```js
let val = 5;
let result = !val;
console.log(result);
// Output: false
```

Q9) Predict the output:

```js
let a = 10;
let b = 20;
let result = !(a && b);
console.log(result);
// Output: false
```

Q10) Predict the output:

```js
let x = 0;
let y = 1;
let result = !(x || y);
console.log(result);
// Output: false
```

